---
status: 'published';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Web Builders Guide - Pick a platform that fits how you work"
  description="A calm, vendor-light overview to help you choose a website platform based on goals, update rhythm, and maintenance appetite."
>
  <!-- Hero with background image (fixed stacking) -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <img
        src="/images/guides/gold-circles.webp"
        alt=""
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-40 dark:opacity-50"
      />
      <div
        class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-white/85 via-white/60 to-white/20 dark:from-gray-950/85 dark:via-gray-950/70 dark:to-gray-950/40"
      >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative z-10">
      <div
        class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-24 md:py-32 text-center"
      >
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 mb-2"
        >
          Guides
        </p>
        <h1
          class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
        >
          Web Builders Guide
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          The goal is not to pick a trendy tool. It is to choose a stable
          platform that supports your outcomes, update rhythm, and maintenance
          preferences. Specific tool choices happen in conversation. This page
          frames how to decide.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section: Quick orientation -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        Quick orientation
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Astro (custom, fast)
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-2">
            <li>
              Great for small, crafted sites where performance, structure, and
              longevity matter.
            </li>
            <li>Edits can be file-based or through a light CMS added later.</li>
            <li>Best when layouts are stable and changes are purposeful.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            WordPress (familiar, flexible)
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-2">
            <li>
              Solid for ongoing publishing and when non-technical editing
              matters.
            </li>
            <li>
              Large ecosystem; needs mindful curation and light maintenance.
            </li>
            <li>
              Light ecommerce with WooCommerce works well for small catalogs;
              larger or more complex shops are evaluated case-by-case (often
              with a partner).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Visual builders (template-driven)
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-2">
            <li>Fast to launch and edit in the browser.</li>
            <li>
              Strong fit for simple sites, landing pages, and DIY changes.
            </li>
            <li>Less control over deep structure and performance details.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-3">
            Examples: Webflow, Framer, Squarespace. Examples only — we will
            choose the simplest tool that fits your outcomes and how you will
            edit.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-4">
        I primarily build custom sites in Astro and WordPress. I can
        design/structure and hand off in visual builders; heavier builds get a
        specialist referral.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Decorative band -->
  <div class="relative">
    <img
      src="/images/guides/dots-blue-yellow-tws-thin.webp"
      alt=""
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="w-full h-24 object-cover opacity-85 dark:opacity-70"
    />
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 ring-1 ring-stone-200/70 dark:ring-stone-800/70 pointer-events-none"
    >
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section: Map your choice -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        Map your choice
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            By outcomes
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Inquiries and credibility: one-page or light multi-section site.
            </li>
            <li>
              Portfolio trust: case studies, visuals, and a clear process page.
            </li>
            <li>
              Content visibility: articles and resources that compound over
              time.
            </li>
            <li>
              Transactions or integrations: add modules or choose a suite with
              those built-in.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            By update rhythm
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Rarely: keep it simple and durable.</li>
            <li>
              Monthly: maintain a small set of pages and a cadence for updates.
            </li>
            <li>
              Weekly: choose an editor that feels natural; keep the structure
              tidy.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section: How editing works -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        How editing works
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Astro
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Content can live in simple files or a light CMS. Edits are
            intentional, releases are clean, and performance stays strong.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            WordPress
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Edit in the browser with a block editor. Good for adding posts,
            light pages, and updates without touching code.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Visual builders
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Edit layouts and text directly in the browser. Best when you want to
            change copy or sections yourself.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-3">
        We can also connect a privacy-first analytics view and a simple form or
        booking page. No heavy tracking by default.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section: When to choose which -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        When to choose which
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              Astro: you want speed, tight structure, and a site that ages well
              with small purposeful changes.
            </li>
            <li>
              WordPress: you plan to publish content and want a familiar browser
              editor.
            </li>
            <li>
              Visual builder: you want a fast start and expect to tweak layouts
              yourself.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>
              If you need memberships, courses, or robust e-commerce, we will
              evaluate options together and bring in a specialist when it helps.
            </li>
            <li>
              If you need a complex web app, we will refer you to a developer
              with that focus.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section: Micro‑FAQ -->
  <section
    id="faq"
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2
        class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4"
      >
        Common questions
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Can I edit it myself?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Yes. WordPress and visual builders are browser‑editable. Astro can
            be file‑based or paired with a light CMS.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Which is best for SEO?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Clear structure and readable pages matter more than platform. We
            keep it fast, accessible, and organized.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article
          class="rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 p-6"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Do you build in Webflow/Squarespace?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            For straightforward sites, yes. For app‑like needs or heavy
            commerce, we will bring in a specialist.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section: Next steps -->
  <section
    class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="/guides"
          class="inline-block bg-blue-700 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-800 transition dark:bg-blue-500 dark:hover:bg-blue-400"
        >
          Back to Guides
        </a>
        <a
          href="/guides/planning"
          class="inline-block border border-blue-700 text-blue-700 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-50 transition dark:border-blue-300 dark:text-blue-300 dark:hover:bg-blue-900/30"
        >
          Open Planning
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-3">
        We will finalize tool choices together based on your goals and
        maintenance appetite.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
